subproblems.statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ, μ a measure on ℝ^P, and M, E ⊆ ℝ^P Borel. Let S_j ⊆ M (j ∈ ℕ) be pairwise disjoint Borel sets with μ(M ∖ ⋃_j S_j) = 0. Let u_k : ℝ^P → ℝ (k ∈ ℕ) and v, D : ℝ^P → ℝ satisfy:
- D is μ-integrable on M;
- each u_k is a.e. strongly measurable for μ⌞M;
- for every k, |u_k(x)| ≤ D(x) for μ-a.e. x ∈ M;
- v is μ-integrable on M ∩ E.
Suppose that for every j, ∫_{S_j} u_k dμ → ∫_{S_j ∩ E} v dμ as k → ∞. Then ∫_M u_k dμ → ∫_{M∩E} v dμ as k → ∞. All integrals are Bochner integrals.
